  "Question": "For real numbers \\(x\\) and \\(y,\\) define \\[x \\spadesuit y = (x + y)(x - y).\\] What is \\(3 \\spadesuit (4 \\spadesuit 5)?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(-72\\)",
    "B": "\\(-27\\)",
    "C": "\\(-24\\)",
    "D": "\\(24\\)",
    "E": "\\(72\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "Evaluate the parenthesized operation first, using the stated definition:\n\\[\n4\\spadesuit 5=(4+5)(4-5)=9(-1)=-9.\n\\]\nThis result becomes the second input of the outer operation, so\n\\[\n3\\spadesuit(-9)=(3+(-9))(3-(-9))=(-6)(12)=-72.\n\\]\nTherefore the value is \\(-72\\), choice A.",
